      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. Even with normal kidney and liver function, this raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a rationale for the order note. I would still want to be sure it isn't a typo."
      }
